1
00:00:03,850 --> 00:00:06,410
I'll do just what you wished for.

2
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,640
Yuka-chan...

3
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:15,610
You can't escape from here.

4
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,230
Everyone will definitely die.

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:19,810
That's why...

6
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:23,690
Until our final moments...

7
00:00:23,730 --> 00:00:25,780
...we will be siblings.

8
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:31,570
You don't want to be killed by the ghosts here, right?

9
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,060
Don't worry.

10
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:35,270
I won't let that happen.

11
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:38,490
I will protect you from such fate.

12
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:42,430
And..I will be the one to end it...

13
00:00:42,430 --> 00:00:45,890
You...and that tiny life of yours that is.

14
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:54,880
This one is pretty big!

15
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,330
Kishinuma-kun!

16
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:11,840
Hello?

17
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:19,960
....ple..ase...

18
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:22,840
Naomi?

19
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:24,800
Mom?!

20
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:25,990
Is that you, Naomi?

21
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:28,190
Answer me, Naomi!

22
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:30,190
Mom, It's me!

23
00:01:30,190 --> 00:01:31,900
Something terrible happened and-

24
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:34,560
Naomi! Let me at least hear your voice! Please!

25
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:37,980
Mom?!

26
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:39,850
Can't you hear my voice?!

27
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:40,890
Mom!

28
00:01:40,890 --> 00:01:43,240
Please! Say something!

29
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:46,160
It's your mom, Naomi!

30
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:47,850
Mom! Mom!

31
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:16,220
In this incident...

32
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:18,950
Only one girl was saved...

33
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:21,850
Shinozaki Sachiko.

34
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:25,100
That's the girl from before!

35
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:26,710
But that's weird...

36
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:29,100
She wasn't killed.

37
00:04:29,870 --> 00:04:33,480
And yet, why does she exist here as a ghost?

38
00:04:34,590 --> 00:04:36,140
I'm worried about Yuka.

39
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:38,520
She could be with that girl right now...

40
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,620
A video tape?

41
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:43,940
Coverage?

42
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:45,640
It's fairly recent!

43
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,740
Along with this notebook...

44
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:55,350
"Shinozaki Sachiko Charm".

45
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:59,170
"Reverse Law… Ritual Memo"?

46
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,060
Isn't this...

47
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,470
a way to get back to our original world?!

48
00:05:06,750 --> 00:05:09,220
I'll be over there in a moment...

49
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:11,100
No!!

50
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:13,100
Onii-chan!!

51
00:05:14,970 --> 00:05:16,370
Wait for me!

52
00:05:16,370 --> 00:05:18,620
Your big brother is right here, isn't he?!

53
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,730
Onee-chan, this way..

54
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:27,820
Wait!

55
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:29,180
Yuka-chan...

56
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:31,070
My cute little sister...

57
00:05:31,070 --> 00:05:32,620
Where did you go?!

58
00:05:32,810 --> 00:05:34,310
Be a good girl, Yuka!

59
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:36,020
Come here!

60
00:05:37,530 --> 00:05:39,500
I'll kill you, I swear I will!

61
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:41,110
I'll kill you, Yuka!

62
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:52,070
Looks like I'm locked in...

63
00:05:52,170 --> 00:05:54,230
I even found a way to go back!

64
00:05:54,810 --> 00:05:57,600
Like hell I'm going to let this stop me!

65
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:00,360
Wait for me...Yuka...everyone...

66
00:06:00,550 --> 00:06:02,830
To be able to worry so much about another's well-being

67
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,650
that it torments you to the core...

68
00:06:06,970 --> 00:06:11,250
It's an exquisite stigmata that affects the living and dead like.

69
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:12,920
Who are you...?

70
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:15,690
I'm a ghost of a girl who died here.

71
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:17,610
I see...

72
00:06:17,610 --> 00:06:19,860
Happiness and unhappiness are linked.

73
00:06:20,030 --> 00:06:22,510
Whenever one attempts to gain
good fortune with little effort,

74
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:24,750
there is always a risk.

75
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:28,810
You and your friends were trapped in this school

76
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:32,650
because you performed the Sachiko
Ever After charm and messed it up.

77
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:33,950
Messed it up?!

78
00:06:34,350 --> 00:06:37,780
One of you chanted the phrase too many times, or too few.

79
00:06:38,430 --> 00:06:41,370
It did not match the number of people present.

80
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:43,450
Someone...

81
00:06:43,450 --> 00:06:44,790
There's no way that happened!

82
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,960
I'm sure I counted it nine times!

83
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:49,080
You might have done so but,

84
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:51,580
what about the friends you were with?

85
00:06:52,190 --> 00:06:55,670
One of your friends might have thought it was a pain in the ass to count it...

86
00:06:56,160 --> 00:07:00,530
or they simply didn't want the fun
to end and flubbed it on purpose...

87
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,050
Even if it wasn't on purpose,

88
00:07:03,050 --> 00:07:07,510
some of your friends have a tendency not to take things very seriously, no?

89
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:11,460
"Oh well! No one will find out anyways."

90
00:07:12,310 --> 00:07:16,160
Without even realizing their actions
would lead to this terrible situation...

91
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,610
That's enough!

92
00:07:18,690 --> 00:07:20,370
Perhaps it's because of the nature of my job...

93
00:07:20,610 --> 00:07:23,500
I couldn't help myself and prepared far too many likely scenarios.

94
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:28,600
You still have your piece of the charm, right?

95
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:32,120
Grasp it firmly with your hands and think...

96
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:34,950
...about those dear to you...

97
00:07:35,210 --> 00:07:37,520
Sorry, I'm in a hurry.

98
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,640
Such concern for your friends...

99
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:41,770
spurs your heart into action...

100
00:07:41,970 --> 00:07:43,500
It's truly a noble sentiment.

101
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:47,440
A charm is simply a representation
of one's feelings for another.

102
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:49,000
Something of the heart.

103
00:07:49,570 --> 00:07:52,060
Be it love or hatred,

104
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:53,750
the stronger the emotions,

105
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:56,560
the more powerful the charm will become.

106
00:07:58,650 --> 00:07:59,720
W-What?

107
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:03,090
Those in our way will not be forgiven.

108
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:05,090
They will suffer.

109
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,060
S-Stop!

110
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:17,080
Go...to the one who fills your thoughts.

111
00:08:17,390 --> 00:08:20,630
Though, you might already be too late...

112
00:08:28,470 --> 00:08:30,620
Did I lose consciousness?

113
00:08:33,550 --> 00:08:35,310
T-This place is...

114
00:08:36,010 --> 00:08:37,890
our classroom, isn't it?!

115
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:42,140
Shinozaki!

116
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:43,270
Get a grip!

117
00:08:43,350 --> 00:08:45,170
Hey! Shinozaki!

118
00:08:52,970 --> 00:08:54,880
K-Kishinuma-kun...

119
00:08:58,700 --> 00:08:59,740
No way!

120
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:01,160
It's true!

121
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:03,600
We made it back, didn't we?!

122
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,490
Yeah!

123
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:08,500
Satoshi, Yui-sensei and the others...

124
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,020
...did not make it back yet.

125
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:11,820
What's wrong?!

126
00:09:13,050 --> 00:09:14,870
T-That...

127
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:20,330
What the hell...is that?

128
00:09:20,330 --> 00:09:22,660
Don't tell me, it's not over yet?!

129
00:09:35,090 --> 00:09:36,420
Damn it! Stay away!

130
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:39,780
It was a rainy evening after school, just like this one...

131
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:42,970
On the morning of the day I was kidnapped,

132
00:09:43,290 --> 00:09:45,790
I got into a fight with my mom.

133
00:09:46,190 --> 00:09:48,030
W-What are you talking about?

134
00:09:48,030 --> 00:09:50,290
I didn't want to see her face...

135
00:09:50,290 --> 00:09:53,610
so after school, I decided that instead of going home...

136
00:09:53,610 --> 00:09:55,720
I would wait a little in the hallway near the lockers,

137
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,520
and watch the rain.

138
00:09:57,870 --> 00:10:01,800
That's when Yoshikazu-sensei came and sat next to me.

139
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,020
"Uh-huh",

140
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:05,490
he listened to me while nodding.

141
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:09,270
Sensei was sick and couldn't speak much, you see...

142
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:11,430
but he had a very kind heart.

143
00:10:11,430 --> 00:10:12,990
I liked him.

144
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:14,410
But...

145
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,060
Onii-san...

146
00:10:17,090 --> 00:10:17,950
Onee-san...

147
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,040
I'm sorry.

148
00:10:22,770 --> 00:10:23,880
You're...

149
00:10:24,910 --> 00:10:27,540
You're Kanno Yuki-chan, right?

150
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:30,130
Thank you for before.

151
00:10:30,490 --> 00:10:34,110
For making the effort, to help us, who were killed in that school.

152
00:10:34,390 --> 00:10:36,590
So why are you still here?

153
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:39,090
Didn't we put you to rest already?!

154
00:10:39,590 --> 00:10:40,530
That's...

155
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:42,700
I'm sorry, we're still...

156
00:10:44,030 --> 00:10:46,190
We returned your tongues and

157
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:50,180
we made the culprit confess his horrible crimes but as I thought, there's still-

158
00:10:50,170 --> 00:10:51,320
That wasn't enough.

159
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:53,260
The culprit's confession...

160
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:58,590
Are you saying that the confession
from his doll wasn't enough?

161
00:10:59,690 --> 00:11:01,530
That's...not...

162
00:11:01,530 --> 00:11:05,730
Why do you feel the need to trap
so many innocent people in there?

163
00:11:06,370 --> 00:11:10,820
You kids are the ones who brought us there, right?

164
00:11:11,010 --> 00:11:12,440
That's wrong.

165
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:17,460
We're just the gears that keep the closed spaces together...

166
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:21,250
You've all killed several people there already, haven't you?!

167
00:11:21,250 --> 00:11:22,020
Wait!

168
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:24,020
Let's hear her out.

169
00:11:25,170 --> 00:11:26,370
Fine...

170
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:30,820
Even if it's just the two of you, I'm glad I was able to get you back to safety.

171
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:34,330
Why the hell are you suddenly so concerned about us?!

172
00:11:34,890 --> 00:11:36,070
I've heard about this before.

173
00:11:37,570 --> 00:11:42,400
A spirit whose life ended violently and abruptly, leaving behind regrets...

174
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:48,610
To normal people, it's kind of like stopping short at the edge of madness.

175
00:11:49,260 --> 00:11:51,820
That's why all sorts of thoughts and feelings

176
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:53,960
are swirling around in your head...

177
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:56,970
So this girl and the other one are
two sides of the same coin, huh?

178
00:11:57,560 --> 00:12:00,730
Then please! Bring the other living ones,

179
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:03,370
Mochida-kun and the others, back!

180
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:05,500
I'm afraid that's impossible.

181
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:07,440
Why?

182
00:12:07,650 --> 00:12:10,070
Back there, the power of the curse wavered...

183
00:12:10,070 --> 00:12:12,920
so I took that chance to bring you both here.

184
00:12:13,410 --> 00:12:14,130
But...

185
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:17,560
Because of the sadness and despair that lurks there....

186
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:21,860
It began feeding on those connected to it.

187
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,600
It won't be long...

188
00:12:23,730 --> 00:12:29,270
...before I turn back into a vengeful sprint who attacks people without mercy.

189
00:12:30,290 --> 00:12:32,280
Then that's more of a reason to hurry!

190
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:36,730
Isn't there any way to save Mochida-kun and the others?!

191
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,780
There is only one way.

192
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:40,470
What do we need to do?

193
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:42,840
I'm sure you already know.

194
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,180
You'll have to return to that place

195
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:48,170
and if you can put us all to rest then

196
00:12:48,380 --> 00:12:52,720
the closed spaces, upon losing its gears, will probably disappear.

197
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:54,970
We have to go back there again?!

198
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:55,950
Hey...

199
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,350
Why did you stop halfway before?

200
00:12:59,950 --> 00:13:01,800
I didn't want to remember it.

201
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:05,420
But if you really want to know, I'll tell you.

202
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:07,160
What happened that time.

203
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:13,500
Shinozaki!

204
00:13:16,410 --> 00:13:19,370
Shinozaki!

205
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:21,870
Huh?

206
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,810
What happened to me?

207
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:26,940
I should have passed out, yet why do I still feel conscious?

208
00:13:27,430 --> 00:13:29,100
But it's pitch black...

209
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:31,100
I can't move my body...

210
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:39,580
This place...

211
00:13:39,850 --> 00:13:41,770
It's a room I never saw before...

212
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:52,690
No! Stop!!

213
00:13:53,230 --> 00:13:54,690
What are you doing?!

214
00:13:54,690 --> 00:13:56,690
Why are you blindfolding me?!

215
00:13:56,690 --> 00:13:57,540
Take it off!

216
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:59,010
In or..der...

217
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:00,680
Order?!

218
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,550
No! Stop! Stop-

219
00:14:06,230 --> 00:14:08,570
...can't see! I can't see!

220
00:14:19,610 --> 00:14:20,550
No more!

221
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:46,160
Stop...just stop already...I'm begging you!

222
00:14:50,530 --> 00:14:51,090
Huh?

223
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:54,090
My...teeth...

224
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:59,320
N-No! Stop! Stop!!

225
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,320
Sa-

226
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:10,030
Sachiko...

227
00:15:14,110 --> 00:15:15,010
Why?

228
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:18,300
Why are you the...

229
00:15:25,830 --> 00:15:27,750
Will it come out?~

230
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:31,850
Shinozaki...

231
00:15:32,250 --> 00:15:33,970
Snap out of it, Shinozaki!

232
00:15:33,970 --> 00:15:34,960
Shinozaki!!

233
00:15:36,150 --> 00:15:37,640
Are you alright, Shinozaki?

234
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:43,360
That's all I can show you from back then.

235
00:15:44,070 --> 00:15:45,500
Did you see something?

236
00:15:47,230 --> 00:15:51,230
The culprit who...killed...those kids...

237
00:15:54,060 --> 00:15:56,950
The murderer's confession...we had the wrong person...

238
00:15:56,950 --> 00:15:58,010
What did you say?!

239
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:04,480
Just now...I was in Yuki-chan's place...and was killed.

240
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,480
Shinozaki...

241
00:16:07,580 --> 00:16:08,970
The murderer is...

242
00:16:09,630 --> 00:16:13,760
The one whose picture we saw in that old newspaper...

243
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:16,780
That girl in the red dress...

244
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:19,040
Shinozaki Sachiko!

245
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:24,450
No...

246
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:26,220
That can't be right...

247
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:30,230
How the hell could she kidnap kids her age and lock them up?

248
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:32,500
It's gotta be the teacher-

249
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:34,520
Yoshikazu was just an accomplice.

250
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:37,830
When these children were killed by Sachiko...

251
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:40,710
He was cowering in the corner of the room.

252
00:16:40,950 --> 00:16:41,890
Seriously?

253
00:16:43,610 --> 00:16:47,920
I don't know the reason why he helped her, but...

254
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:50,390
We have to tell Mochida-kun and the others!

255
00:16:50,860 --> 00:16:54,560
If they run into Sachiko, they could be in danger!

256
00:16:54,790 --> 00:16:56,270
Y-Yeah...

257
00:16:56,270 --> 00:16:57,390
I guess...

258
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,690
Even Naho-san wasn't able to find out the whole truth,

259
00:16:59,690 --> 00:17:01,780
and she's been in there longer than any of us!

260
00:17:02,050 --> 00:17:04,250
We have to hurry and tell everyone know the truth,

261
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:06,460
before they are all killed!

262
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:07,830
Yuki-chan! Please!

263
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:10,430
Take us to that place once more!

264
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:15,900
You and the others, we'll definitely put you all to rest!

265
00:17:16,310 --> 00:17:18,850
But...I wouldn't recommend that...

266
00:17:19,270 --> 00:17:22,740
Because of you and your friends,

267
00:17:22,890 --> 00:17:26,330
the spaces have become unbalanced.

268
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,330
If you go back there now...

269
00:17:28,950 --> 00:17:29,740
Yuki-chan...

270
00:17:30,390 --> 00:17:35,640
I don't think I would be able to bring
you two back here again...

271
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:37,590
H-Hey!

272
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:38,870
Wait a minute!

273
00:17:38,990 --> 00:17:40,980
Are seriously intending to go back there?!

274
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,590
Let's go, Kishinuma-kun!

275
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:44,210
To save everyone!

276
00:17:44,210 --> 00:17:45,050
Okay?

277
00:17:45,050 --> 00:17:45,730
Mochida-kun and-

278
00:17:45,730 --> 00:17:46,910
Count me out!

279
00:17:47,670 --> 00:17:50,160
I never want to go to that place again!

280
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:51,770
Kishinuma-kun?

281
00:17:51,870 --> 00:17:54,630
Going back there is just fucking insane!

282
00:17:55,130 --> 00:17:57,490
This time we might really die, you know!

283
00:17:57,830 --> 00:17:58,910
Why?!

284
00:17:59,050 --> 00:18:00,870
As long as you're safe, it's alright?!

285
00:18:00,870 --> 00:18:02,510
Now's not the time to be talking like that!

286
00:18:02,510 --> 00:18:03,600
We may die there!

287
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:05,340
You don't want to die, right?!

288
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:10,770
Of course I'm worried about Satoshi and the others...

289
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:11,670
But-

290
00:18:11,670 --> 00:18:12,450
That's enough!

291
00:18:12,470 --> 00:18:14,250
I guess I was wrong about you!

292
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:15,860
I'll go by myself!

293
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:16,560
Then I'll-

294
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:17,780
I can't believe you!

295
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:20,120
Don't you want to save your friends?!

296
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:22,750
I know it's dangerous, but!

297
00:18:23,630 --> 00:18:25,830
Mochida-kun would definitely do the same!

298
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:27,720
Heartless bastard!

299
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:28,460
Egoist!

300
00:18:28,590 --> 00:18:29,500
Delinquent!

301
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:30,380
Mochida-kun and the others-

302
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:31,500
Shut the fuck up!!

303
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:33,680
Without knowing how I feel...

304
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:37,250
You don't want to save everyone, just Satoshi, right?!

305
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:38,830
Knock it off already!

306
00:18:38,830 --> 00:18:40,050
I'm at my limit....

307
00:18:40,050 --> 00:18:41,910
Mochida! Mochida! Mochida! Mochida!!

308
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:44,340
It's fine! I don't care who you like!

309
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:45,000
But this-

310
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,650
Stop it! Why would you say something like that?!

311
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:51,310
Mochida-kun isn't the only one I'm worried about, you know!

312
00:18:57,660 --> 00:18:58,540
Yuki-chan...

313
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:00,420
Please...

314
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:03,240
I don't care if it's just me, take me back there!

315
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:06,200
I understand.

316
00:19:10,470 --> 00:19:12,790
Just so you know, Kishinuma-kun...

317
00:19:12,790 --> 00:19:14,620
I'm scared too!

318
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:25,510
Damn it!

319
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:28,820
Why did things end up like this...?!

320
00:19:32,630 --> 00:19:34,370
Where did I fall?

321
00:19:35,430 --> 00:19:37,330
It's too dark to see anything...

322
00:19:41,130 --> 00:19:42,750
The light from my cellphone!

323
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,080
I just...

324
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:50,790
You're completely alone.

325
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:01,120
Huh?

326
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:02,880
Where is this place?

327
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:08,710
This is Naomi's...

328
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:13,250
Is there someone down there?

329
00:20:18,970 --> 00:20:19,750
Naomi?

330
00:20:21,370 --> 00:20:22,360
Is that you, Naomi?!

331
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:26,260
Are you alright, Naomi?!

332
00:20:27,310 --> 00:20:28,590
What happened?

333
00:20:31,090 --> 00:20:31,980
Naomi?

334
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:38,670
Stupid! You should have come sooner!

335
00:20:38,670 --> 00:20:39,660
Satoshi!

336
00:20:39,660 --> 00:20:41,780
Satoshi!!

337
00:20:42,230 --> 00:20:43,740
N-Naomi?

338
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:52,220
It looks like you injured your leg.

339
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:54,960
Yeah, but it's fine now.

340
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:57,260
Seiko patched it up for me.

341
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:58,910
Shinohara?

342
00:20:59,190 --> 00:21:00,990
Where is she?

343
00:21:01,110 --> 00:21:02,310
You're not together?

344
00:21:03,510 --> 00:21:05,860
Seiko...Seiko is...

345
00:21:10,370 --> 00:21:12,650
We split up after an argument.

346
00:21:12,890 --> 00:21:14,650
It was my fault...

347
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:19,010
Next time I saw her, she was hanging...

348
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:21,570
It may be all my fault...

349
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:23,440
Because I said those awful things...

350
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:26,210
I can't even apologize now...

351
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:30,090
It's alright, it's not your fault.

352
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:33,660
I'm sure Shinohara wasn't her usual self.

353
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:36,060
Satoshi...

354
00:21:36,580 --> 00:21:40,750
You should know best that Shinohara wouldn't give up so easily and commit suicide, right?

355
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:48,400
I'm sorry, Shinohara...

356
00:21:48,650 --> 00:21:50,890
We would like to take you with us but...

357
00:21:54,710 --> 00:21:57,020
Looks like it's safe for now.

358
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:00,700
What happened to you?!

359
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:07,740
Who do you think you're talking to, you foolish woman?!

360
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:11,310
I'll carve out that filthy tongue of yours!

361
00:22:35,050 --> 00:22:37,230
I'll just hide them here...

362
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:44,550
It's a little breezy, but...

363
00:22:44,620 --> 00:22:47,030
I don't want to wear them while they are wet...

364
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:54,840
I was looking for you, Yuka!

365
00:23:05,060 --> 00:23:06,760
Mochida-kun!

366
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,590
Nakashima-san!

367
00:23:08,590 --> 00:23:10,040
Shinohara-san!

368
00:23:11,450 --> 00:23:12,740
That uniform is...

369
00:23:15,850 --> 00:23:17,170
Morishige-kun...

370
00:23:22,150 --> 00:23:22,790
Yuka!

371
00:23:22,930 --> 00:23:25,030
Satoshi, I'm fine

372
00:23:25,030 --> 00:23:26,760
so hurry up and go to where Yuka-chan is!

373
00:23:27,750 --> 00:23:29,670
Stop it!!

374
00:23:30,070 --> 00:23:31,260
Let me go!!

375
00:23:33,220 --> 00:23:36,100
I wonder what kind of screams you will make, Yuka.

376
00:23:41,980 --> 00:23:43,270
Yukaaa!!

377
00:23:57,370 --> 00:24:00,400
What's this? Already finished?

378
00:24:01,540 --> 00:24:02,740
I see...

379
00:24:22,370 --> 00:24:23,110
Yuka!

380
00:24:26,280 --> 00:24:28,110
Hang in there! I'll-

381
00:24:34,070 --> 00:24:35,300
You bastard...

382
00:24:42,990 --> 00:24:43,910
Yuka-chan!

383
00:24:45,990 --> 00:24:47,240
Is that you, Shinozaki?!

384
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:48,940
Kishinuma-kun?! Why?

385
00:24:49,170 --> 00:24:50,860
Take care of Yuka!

386
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:52,250
Got it!

387
00:25:02,650 --> 00:25:03,890
Kishinuma-kun!

388
00:25:03,890 --> 00:25:05,640
Run! Shinozaki!

389
00:25:06,980 --> 00:25:07,490
But-

390
00:25:07,490 --> 00:25:08,480
Hurry up and run!

391
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:11,110
For whose sake do you think I came back for?!

392
00:25:14,400 --> 00:25:14,980
I-

393
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:24,900
Kishinuma-kun!

394
00:25:26,010 --> 00:25:26,970
Hurry...

395
00:25:27,730 --> 00:25:29,630
Hurry up and run!!

396
00:25:35,910 --> 00:25:36,630
Yuka!

397
00:25:37,770 --> 00:25:39,940
Shinozaki! Yuka!

398
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:41,620
What happened?!

399
00:25:42,930 --> 00:25:43,740
Yoshiki?!

400
00:25:51,230 --> 00:25:53,000
W-We have to run, Shinozaki!

401
00:25:59,650 --> 00:26:00,470
Yuka...

402
00:26:02,720 --> 00:26:04,610
Onii...chan...

403
00:26:06,130 --> 00:26:12,450
...Let's..go..home..together...